WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:01.610
- See, Sarah Lynn?

00:00:01.610 --> 00:00:02.443
We're not doomed.

00:00:02.443 --> 00:00:04.600
In the great, grand scheme of things

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.310
we're just tiny specks that
will one day be forgotten.

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:10.200
So it doesn't matter
what we did in the past

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.010
or how we'll be remembered.

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:15.580
The only thing that matters
is right now, this moment.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:19.570
This one spectacular moment
we are sharing together.

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.470
Right, Sarah Lynn?

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:23.493
Sarah Lynn?

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.500
- You're responsible for
your own happiness, you know?

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:27.950
- Good Lord, that's depressing.

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:28.910
- No it's not!

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:30.360
- I'm responsible for my own happiness?

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.360
I can't even be responsible
for my own breakfast.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.840
You're a real stupid piece of shit.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:36.260
But I know I'm a piece of shit.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.180
That at least makes me better
than all the pieces of shit

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.070
who don't they're pieces of shit.

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:40.940
Or is it worse?

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:41.773
Breakfast.

00:00:41.773 --> 00:00:43.260
You're a real stupid piece of shit

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.320
and everywhere you go you destroy people.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:46.290
Of course your mother never loved you,

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:47.123
what do you expect?

00:00:47.123 --> 00:00:48.060
That's why Sarah Lynn died,

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:49.465
that's why Charlotte
will never forgive you,

00:00:49.465 --> 00:00:50.298
what are you gonna do to Hollyhock?

00:00:50.298 --> 00:00:51.740
What are you gonna do, asshole?

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:52.860
Shut up!

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:55.440
If I'm shitty, that's
just because I'm shitty

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:56.730
and you're allowed to be mad at me.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:58.380
But you need to know that whatever I do,

00:00:58.380 --> 00:00:59.883
it's not your fault.

00:01:02.117 --> 00:01:03.490
- I know.

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:07.100
I mean, I know, but I don't
always know, you know?

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.400
Like sometimes I have this tiny
voice in the back of my head

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.597
that goes like "hey, everyone hates you

00:01:11.597 --> 00:01:13.647
"and they're not wrong to feel that way."

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:15.730
- I know what you mean.

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:18.630
- That voice, the one that
tells you you're worthless

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:20.623
and stupid and ugly,
- Yeah?

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:23.000
- It goes away right?

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.830
It's just like a dumb
teenage girl thing but

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:26.853
then it goes away?

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:28.793
- Yeah.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.110
Don't you get it?

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:34.460
This is my last chance to
make people love me again.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.720
If this goes out everybody's
gonna see the real me.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:38.880
Now I spent a lot of
time with the real me,

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:41.250
and believe me, nobody's
gonna love that guy.

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.083
- Okay.

00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:43.890
Now if you'll excuse me I
need to go take a shower

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:45.530
so I can't tell if I'm crying or not.

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:48.350
I don't understand how people live.

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:50.350
It's amazing to me that
people wake up every morning

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:54.060
and say "yeah, another day, let's do it."

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:55.730
How do people do it?

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:57.230
I don't know how.

00:01:57.230 --> 00:01:59.770
So I stopped at a Jack in
the Box on the way here

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:02.177
and the girl behind
the counter said "hiya,

00:02:02.177 --> 00:02:03.970
"are you having an awesome day?"

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:05.660
Not "how are you doing today?"

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:08.020
No, "are you having an awesome day?"

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:09.500
Which is pretty shitty,

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:11.610
because it puts the onus
on me to disagree with her,

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.800
like if I'm not having an awesome day

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.910
suddenly I'm the negative one.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:17.430
Usually when people ask how I'm doing

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:19.270
the real answer is I'm doing shitty.

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:20.620
But I can't say I'm doing shitty

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:22.690
because I don't even have a
good reason to be doing shitty,

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:24.500
so if I say "I'm doing shitty",

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:26.180
then they say "why, what's wrong?"

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:28.930
And I have to be like "I
don't know, all of it?"

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:30.630
So instead when people ask how I'm doing

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:33.900
I usually say "I am doing so great."

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.810
But when this girl at the Jack in the Box

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:37.430
asked me if I was having an awesome day

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:40.047
I thought "well today, I'm
actually allowed to feel shitty.

00:02:40.047 --> 00:02:41.460
"Today I have a good reason."

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.840
So I said to her "well my mom died."

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.200
And she immediately burst into tears.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:49.030
So now I have to comfort
her, which is annoying.

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:51.440
And meanwhile there's a line
of people forming behind me

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.350
who are all giving me
these real judgy looks

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:55.130
because I've made the
Jack in the Box girl cry.

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:57.900
And she's bawling and she's
saying "I'm sorry, I'm so sorry"

00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:59.607
and I'm like "it's fine, it's fine,

00:02:59.607 --> 00:03:02.997
"I mean it's not fine,
but you know, it's fine.

00:03:02.997 --> 00:03:05.127
"And I would like to
order a Double Jack meal

00:03:05.127 --> 00:03:06.687
"and I've kind of got somewhere to be

00:03:06.687 --> 00:03:07.997
"so maybe less with the crying

00:03:07.997 --> 00:03:10.160
"and more with the frying, huh?"

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:12.180
And the girl apologizes, again,

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:14.560
and she offers me a free
churro with my meal.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:17.847
And as I'm leaving I think
"I just got a free churro

00:03:17.847 --> 00:03:19.670
"because my mom died."

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:21.320
No one ever tells you when your mom dies

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:22.390
you get a free churro.

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.040
Maybe because you're skinny,

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.390
and maybe 'cause you're pretty

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:27.310
you're used to getting away with things,

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:29.580
but I want you to know that your actions

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:31.090
have an effect on others,

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:34.020
and I hate you and you
are a horrible person,

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:37.290
and you not understanding
that you're a horrible person

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:40.410
doesn't make you less
of a horrible person.

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:41.900
- Who wants an autograph?

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.320
- He's so stupid he doesn't realize

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:44.860
how miserable he should be.

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:45.870
I envy that.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:47.020
- What happened BoJack?

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:50.130
- Same thing that always happens.

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:52.893
You didn't know me then
you fell in love with me.

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:54.730
And now you know me.

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:59.040
- You know, it's funny.

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:01.490
When you look at someone
through rose-colored classes

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:03.993
all the red flags just look like flags.

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:08.550
- I guess my question is do you,

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:10.420
do you think it's too late for me?

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:11.290
- What?

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.330
- I mean, am I just doomed

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:14.790
to be the person that I am,

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:16.240
the person in that book?

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:18.210
It's not too late for me, is it?

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:19.970
It's not too late,

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:21.990
Diane I need you to tell
me that it's not too late.

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:23.420
- BoJack, I--

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:25.420
- I need you to tell me
that I'm a good person.

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:27.300
I know that I can be
selfish and narcicisstic

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:30.010
and self-destructive but
underneath all that, deep down,

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:32.920
I'm a good person and I need
you to tell me that I'm good.

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:33.753
Diane?

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:37.313
Tell me, please Diane,
tell me that I'm good.

00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:43.720
I feel like I was born with a leak.

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:45.240
And any goodness I started with

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:48.250
just slowly spilled out of
me and now it's all gone.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:50.130
And I'll never get it back in me.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:50.963
It's too late.

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:54.620
Life is a series of
closing doors, isn't it?

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:57.310
Nobody completes anybody,
that's not a real thing.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:04:58.520
If you're lucky enough to find someone

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.610
you can halfway tolerate
you sink your nails in

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:02.230
and you don't let go, no matter what.

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:04.220
- So what, I should just settle?

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:06.100
- Yes, thank you, exactly, settle.

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:08.430
Because otherwise, you're
just gonna get older

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:10.810
and harder and more alone.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:13.140
And you're gonna do everything
you can to fill that hole

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:16.690
with friends and your
career and meaningless sex,

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:18.973
but the hole doesn't get filled.

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:21.880
And one day, you're gonna look around

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:25.010
and you're gonna realize
that everybody loves you

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:26.253
but nobody likes you.

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:29.773
And that is the loneliest
feeling in the world.

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:32.040
- You could never say it to me,

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.510
and you still can't say it to her.

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:34.343
- That's not true.

00:05:34.343 --> 00:05:35.523
I can express feelings.

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:38.783
Nothing on the outside,
nothing on the inside.

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:43.933
My mom died and all I
got was this free churro.

00:05:46.387 --> 00:05:48.460
You know the shittiest
thing about all of this?

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:50.010
Is when that stranger behind the counter

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:53.610
gave me that free churro,
that small act of kindness

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:56.010
showed more compassion
than my mother ever gave me

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:57.690
her entire goddamn life.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:00.520
Like how hard is it to do
something nice for a person?

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:02.900
This woman at the Jack in the Box

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:04.530
didn't even know me.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.200
I'm your son.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:07.573
All I had was you.

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:11.350
Suddenly you realize you'll never have

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:13.090
the good relationship you wanted,

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:14.620
that as long as they were alive,

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:16.140
even though you'd never admit it,

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:19.540
part of you, the stupidest
goddamn part of you

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:22.680
was still holding on to that chance.

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:26.080
And you didn't even realize
until that chance went away.

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:30.750
My mother is dead and
everything is worse now.

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:33.630
Because now I know I
will never have a mother

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:35.877
who looks at me from
across a room and says

00:06:35.877 --> 00:06:39.745
"BoJack Horseman, I see you."

00:06:39.745 --> 00:06:42.162
(soft music)

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:48.320
♪ Janis Ian told it very well ♪

00:06:49.732 --> 00:06:52.166
♪ Janis Joplin told it even better ♪

00:06:52.166 --> 00:06:55.505
(tires screech)

00:06:55.505 --> 00:07:00.338
♪ Billie Holiday even
told it even better ♪

00:07:01.597 --> 00:07:02.593
(horse whinnies)

00:07:02.593 --> 00:07:06.497
♪ We always ♪

00:07:06.497 --> 00:07:10.643
♪ We always ♪

00:07:10.643 --> 00:07:14.143
♪ We always have a story ♪

